      "ourRendering": "kāma — arisen from the guṇa rajas, born of vāsanās laid down before, having sound and the rest for its objects, the great devourer, the enemy — drags this man into the objects of sense: the man who, bound up with prakṛti made of the guṇas as they go on rising and being overborne, has set out for knowledge. This very one, its course blocked, turning into the form of anger towards the conscious beings that are the cause of the blocking, the great evildoer, sets him going in harming others and the like. Know this one — arisen from the guṇa rajas, born along with him, the obstructer of the yoga of knowledge — to be the enemy.",
