      "ourRendering": "What is the strong one, the instigator — that is this kāma. Anger too is just this same one, since it is born of it. ‘From kāma is born anger’ — so it runs, as indeed has been said. Wherever anger has for its occasion the reviling of a teacher and the like, there too, the reviling having devotion for its occasion, it is occasioned by kāma and by nothing else. Those who say otherwise — they, out of confusion, do not know the fine point. And it has been said: ‘Apart from kāma, anger and the rest do not arise at all, in any way whatever’ — so it runs. ‘The great devourer’: for great is what kāma has to enjoy. ‘The great evildoer’, because it is the cause of the great evils, the killing of a brahmin and the rest. The enemy, because it stands against every one of the ends a human life is for.",
