      "ourRendering": "Knowledge, though arisen from śāstra even so, does not shine out for the direct seeing of the supreme self, covered by kāma, for the knower too. How much less for the little-knowing? ‘Shaped as kāma’ — that which goes by the name of kāma, the perpetual enemy. ‘Hard to fill’: for kāma is filled with pain. For the rank of Indra and the rest is not got easily. Even if the rank of Indra and the rest has been reached, one wants again the rank of Brahmā and the rest — and so there is no ‘enough’-mind: hence analá. And it has been said: ‘For knowledge and for Brahman — the smoke of fire; for buddhi — the dirt of a mirror, likewise; and then for the jīva — the caul of the embryo: such indeed is kāma’ — so it runs.",
