      "ourRendering": "The indriyas — hearing and the rest — are five. Taking the body as gross, as outward and as bounded, the learned call them higher, pre-eminent, by reference to their subtlety, their being further in, their extending further and so on. So too, higher than the indriyas is manas, which is of the nature of proposing and doubting. So too: higher than manas, however, is buddhi, which is of the nature of settling a matter. So too: he who is further within than all that can be seen — all that ends with buddhi — whom, the embodied one, kāma, joined with the supports, the indriyas and the rest, deludes by way of the veiling of knowledge, as has been said. But he is beyond buddhi. He is the seer of buddhi: the supreme self.",
